<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Newton Creek Long Loop (from Pocket Creek Sno-Park)</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:200-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:pocket-creek-sno-park (OSM node 6287637025); confidence: high; pdf_page: 202; book_elev_ft: 3800</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.331250" lon="-121.585300"><ele>1151.4</ele><name>Highway 35 bridge over Newton Creek</name><desc>source: OSM Newton Creek waterway (way 720315342) where it passes under OR 35, about 150 m north of the pin; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 202; quote: walk 150 yards north down Highway 35, crossing a bridge, to the trail signs west of the highway</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.330900" lon="-121.589300"><ele>1167.0</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 1</name><desc>source: on the north bank of Newton Creek, about 40 m from the OSM creek line (ways 720315342, 150578135); the ski trail is not mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202; quote: Follow the trail as it winds gently uphill along the creek</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.329700" lon="-121.591600"><ele>1179.4</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, lower creek</name><desc>source: on the north bank of Newton Creek, about 40 m from the OSM creek line (ways 720315342, 150578135); the ski trail is not mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.328700" lon="-121.594800"><ele>1195.6</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 2</name><desc>source: on the north bank of Newton Creek, about 40 m from the OSM creek line (ways 720315342, 150578135); the ski trail is not mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.327700" lon="-121.595800"><ele>1203.6</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 3</name><desc>source: on the north bank of Newton Creek, about 40 m from the OSM creek line (ways 720315342, 150578135); the ski trail is not mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.327100" lon="-121.597300"><ele>1211.4</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, skid roads</name><desc>source: on the north bank of Newton Creek, about 40 m from the OSM creek line (ways 720315342, 150578135); the ski trail is not mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202; quote: In about 0.6 mile you reach a wide, straight road that is followed uphill to its end in a meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.325800" lon="-121.600500"><ele>1229.3</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, wide road</name><desc>source: on the north bank of Newton Creek, about 40 m from the OSM creek line (ways 720315342, 150578135); the ski trail is not mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.325500" lon="-121.603700"><ele>1248.7</ele><name>Newton Creek Trail, meadow</name><desc>source: on the north bank of Newton Creek, about 40 m from the OSM creek line (ways 720315342, 150578135); the ski trail is not mapped; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.325600" lon="-121.605500"><ele>1260.1</ele><name>Klindt's Cutoff bridge</name><desc>source: on Newton Creek, placed so Kate Creek Trail to the Elk Meadows Trail is about the sketch's 1.0 mi; map 42 trail 6; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202; quote: Continue to Klindt's Cutoff. If you cross the creek here to Kate Creek Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.323800" lon="-121.612500"><ele>1290.7</ele><name>Kate Creek Trail, mid</name><desc>source: between Newton and Clark creeks, south of Newton Creek; unmapped trail; confidence: low; pdf_page: 202; quote: cross the bridge at Klindt's Cutoff, ski uphill on Kate Creek Trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.324220" lon="-121.620670"><ele>1325.7</ele><name>Kate Creek / Elk Meadows Trail junction</name><desc>source: east end of OSM 'Old Elk Meadows Trail' (way 146985885); confidence: low; pdf_page: 202; quote: and then uphill on Elk Meadows Trail to the Clark Creek bridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.329090" lon="-121.630840"><ele>1385.9</ele><name>Clark Creek bridge</name><desc>source: OSM junction of Old Elk Meadows Trail and Elk Meadows Trail #645 by Clark Creek (OSM waterway 393309719); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 202; quote: Here, turn left (south) and ski to Hood River Meadows Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.325400" lon="-121.635000"><ele>1380.0</ele><name>Hood River Meadows Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:hood-river-meadows-sno-park; confidence: high; pdf_page: 202; quote: Remove your skis and walk to the snowbank on the far side and ski to Hood River Meadows along the access road's shoulder</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.318628" lon="-121.640377"><ele>1393.6</ele><name>Sahalie Falls (old Highway 35)</name><desc>source: OSM node 3965294335 Sahalie Falls; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 203; quote: Ski up to Sahalie Falls (old Highway 35) and continue to Bennett Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.310320" lon="-121.641850"><ele>1425.2</ele><name>Bennett Pass (Pocket Creek Tie Trail start)</name><desc>source: west end of OSM 'Pocket Creek - Bennet Pass Tie trail 682' (way 475739377), at the Bennett Pass Sno-Park pin; confidence: high; pdf_page: 203; book_elev_ft: 4674; quote: Cross the highway, then ski down the Pocket Creek Tie Trail to the East Fork Trail, a wide road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.329021" lon="-121.586759"><ele>1162.9</ele><name>Pocket Creek Sno-Park (finish)</name><desc>source: as start; confidence: high; pdf_page: 203; quote: continue onto the Pocket Creek Trail, a wide, uninteresting road all the way back to Pocket Creek Sno-Park</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Newton Creek Long Loop (from Pocket Creek Sno-Park)</name><desc>1. Pocket Creek Sno-Park -&gt; Highway 35 bridge over Newton Creek: osm (high), 0.27 mi | 2. Highway 35 bridge over Newton Creek -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 1: straight (low), 0.20 mi | 3. Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 1 -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, lower creek: straight (low), 0.14 mi | 4. Newton Creek Trail, lower creek -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 2: straight (low), 0.17 mi | 5. Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 2 -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 3: straight (low), 0.08 mi | 6. Newton Creek Trail, by the creek 3 -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, skid roads: straight (low), 0.08 mi | 7. Newton Creek Trail, skid roads -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, wide road: straight (low), 0.18 mi | 8. Newton Creek Trail, wide road -&gt; Newton Creek Trail, meadow: straight (low), 0.16 mi | 9. Newton Creek Trail, meadow -&gt; Klindt's Cutoff bridge: straight (low), 0.09 mi | 10. Klindt's Cutoff bridge -&gt; Kate Creek Trail, mid: straight (low), 0.36 mi | 11. Kate Creek Trail, mid -&gt; Kate Creek / Elk Meadows Trail junction: straight (low), 0.40 mi | 12. Kate Creek / Elk Meadows Trail junction -&gt; Clark Creek bridge: osm (medium), 0.67 mi | 13. Clark Creek bridge -&gt; Hood River Meadows Sno-Park: osm (medium), 0.36 mi | 14. Hood River Meadows Sno-Park -&gt; Sahalie Falls (old Highway 35): usfs-road (medium), 0.89 mi | 15. Sahalie Falls (old Highway 35) -&gt; Bennett Pass (Pocket Creek Tie Trail start): usfs-road (medium), 0.87 mi | 16. Bennett Pass (Pocket Creek Tie Trail start) -&gt; Pocket Creek Sno-Park (finish): usfs-trail (medium), 5.18 mi</desc>
